    "body": "Work landed locally on issue/71-robust-axis-fit (a2266af), gating now: new `multiaxis/axis_robust.rs` - after the plain fit, keep the facets whose normal lines meet the candidate axis within the fit's tolerance, refit (and refine) on them for up to 4 rounds; each refit must still pass the full existing judgement, and a plain revolve keeps its fit bit for bit. A 72-segment D20 shaft on G54 with a 5.18 mm keyway read 0.153 mm off (refused) -> 0.000 mm (generates); 10 mm keyway 0.058 -> 0.000. The spindle-law refusal now names the set-aside share and gives move-the-offset advice only for a part that is really misplaced. Tests: lathe_spindle_keyed (2, failed on main) + 2 unit tests. Large keyways still refused as not revolved -> #113.",
